    "title": "pandas.Series.str.encode — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1660.g5f0ebded30 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Series.str.encode#\n\n- \nSeries.str.encode(*encoding* ,*errors='strict'* )[source]#\n- Encode character string in the Series/Index using indicated encoding. Equivalent to `str.encode()` .\n  - Parameters:\n    - **encoding** str\n    - Specifies the encoding to be used.\n    - **errors** str, optional\n    - Specifies the error handling scheme. Possible values are those supported by `str.encode()` .\n  - Returns:\n    - Series/Index of objects\n    - A Series or Index with strings encoded into bytes.\n See also \n  - `Series.str.decode`\n  - Decodes bytes into strings in a Series/Index.\n Examples >>> ser = pd.Series([\"cow\", \"123\", \"()\"]) >>> ser.str.encode(encoding=\"ascii\") 0 b'cow' 1 b'123' 2 b'()' dtype: object",
    "markdown_length": 717,
